package com.xoclassic.app;

/** Offline, account-independent instructions for the controls shipped in this app. */
public final class HelpGuide {
    private HelpGuide(){}
    public static final class Topic {
        public final String title,body;
        private Topic(String title,String body){this.title=title;this.body=body;}
    }
    public static final class Section {
        public final String title,summary;
        public final Topic[] topics;
        private Section(String title,String summary,Topic... topics){this.title=title;this.summary=summary;this.topics=topics;}
    }
    private static Topic topic(String title,String body){return new Topic(title,body);}
    public static final Section[] SECTIONS={
        new Section("Getting started","Sign in, find your way around, and keep the app updated",
            topic("Find your settings","Tap Account on the main page to open Settings. The top underline tabs group related controls. Swipe the tab row sideways if more categories are offscreen.\n\nAccount contains Login, Accounts, Moniker and Session. Your saved accounts keep their existing optional PIN protection. The website selector appears on pages that affect one website.\n\nReading chooses the parent-reply preview mode. Theme contains Themes, Colors and Schedule. Uploads holds the ImgBB credential and file support information. These preferences apply to the app, rather than only one website.\n\nPrivacy contains App lock, Threads and Authors. App lock controls opening the whole app. Threads lists the hidden-thread pool for the selected website. Authors manages hidden thread authors across both websites. Help stays last and has its own categories and topic navigation.\n\nSession keeps website session checks, posting recovery when needed, and Forget current login in a separate removal section. Removing a saved login still asks for confirmation."),
            topic("Export and import settings","Open Account → Updates → Backup. Export settings lets you choose a JSON file destination. Import settings checks the selected file, then asks before applying it. Matching supported settings are replaced; unrelated settings stay unchanged.\n\nBackups include themes and schedules, reply-preview preferences, hidden authors and threads, and saved tabs with reading positions. Hidden threads retain their original expiry. Passwords, saved accounts, session cookies, upload API keys and security settings are excluded. Set those up again after reinstalling.\n\nThe JSON file is readable and may contain thread titles and hidden author names. Keep it private. Older releases from before this feature cannot import it. Unknown fields in supported backups are skipped; unsupported newer formats are rejected without changes."),
            topic("Themes and automatic day/night colors","Open Account → Theme. The Themes subtab selects and manages presets or saved custom themes. Colors groups edits into General, Controls, Threads and Search highlights. Schedule contains the day/night settings. Switching subtabs preserves unfinished color and schedule edits. Default preserves the original appearance; Light, Midnight, Sepia and Ocean are also included. Choose a theme and tap Apply selected theme. Customize selected theme lets you edit interface colors using a picker or six-digit hex values. Give it a custom name and Save and apply. Presets cannot be overwritten. Custom themes can be deleted.\n\nAutomatic switching is off initially. Choose separate day and night themes, set their different start times, turn on Change theme by time of day, and Save schedule. Times use the phone's local time, including when you travel. Switching happens while the app is open or when you return. Applying a theme manually turns automatic switching off.\n\nTheme changes keep your screen and reading position. Photos, videos, documents and external webpages keep their own colors."),
            topic("Sign in for the first time","Open Account → Login. Choose the website you use, then enter both your account name and password. Leave Save login securely on this phone checked if you want to keep the login. Tap Sign in.\n\nSign in again when my session expires allows the app to try your saved login when needed. Website sessions can still expire or be revoked.\n\nThe two websites have separate app sessions and saved logins. Signing in through your ordinary browser does not sign the app in."),
            topic("Where the main controls are","The main page has search, New thread, the open-threads button and Account. All returns to the ordinary board. New replies shows tracked threads with higher reply counts. By you and Poasted in use your signed-in website account.\n\nInside a thread, Back returns to the main page. The ‹ and › beside it move between your own editable posts. The three-dot menu beside the title offers Find in thread and Thread media."),
            topic("Install an update","Open the newer AutoAdmit APK with Android Package Installer and install it as an update. Use an APK from a source you trust.\n\nDo not uninstall the existing app first. An ordinary compatible update keeps local settings, saved accounts and open tabs. Uninstalling or clearing app data removes that local information.\n\nUnsent message drafts are not recovered after closing the app. Finish or copy an important draft before leaving.")
        ),
        new Section("Board & search","Filters, stars, visited links, refreshing and hidden authors",
            topic("Search and return to the board","Enter a phrase and tap Search. Search results replace the normal list. The Search button becomes Clear search in the same place.\n\nTap Clear search to return to the normal All board with an empty search field. To search another phrase while results are open, enter it and use the keyboard's Search action.\n\nAll also returns to the ordinary board. The normal All list aims to show 30 threads after filtering hidden authors; hidden threads do not take up those 30 places."),
            topic("All, New replies, By you and Poasted in","All shows the ordinary board in website order.\n\nNew replies shows threads you have read in this app whose displayed reply count has increased. It is not a list of every new thread or a notification that someone replied specifically to you.\n\nBy you shows threads started by your signed-in website account. Poasted in shows threads you have posted in. These views require an app website session; they are not based on your current posting name."),
            topic("Red stars and visited titles","A red star appears when a tracked thread's reply count rises above the count last marked read in this app. Opening the thread updates that read count. A new star can appear after later replies are detected.\n\nIn New replies, swipe a thread left to mark its current displayed count as read without opening it. It disappears from that list until more replies are detected.\n\nVisited thread titles use lavender; unopened titles stay blue. This app's history is separate from the browser and extension. Background author lookups do not count as visiting a thread."),
            topic("Automatic and pull-to-refresh","The visible board or thread checks for updates about once a minute while the app is in the foreground. The board can reorder as the website changes. Reading position is preserved where possible.\n\nFor an immediate refresh, scroll to the very top, pull down until Release to refresh appears, and let go. A short pull or a gesture starting farther down the page does not refresh.\n\nAutomatic updates pause while the app is in the background and protect active writing and other foreground work. Other open tabs are not continuously refreshed."),
            topic("Hide one thread with Undo","Swipe a thread left on All, Search, By you or Poasted in to hide only that thread. A brief Thread hidden message appears at the bottom with Undo. Tap Undo to restore the latest hidden thread; it is available for about six seconds, or longer when Android accessibility settings request more time.\n\nIn New replies, swipe-left keeps marking the thread as read instead of hiding it. You can hold any board thread and choose Hide this thread when you want to hide it individually.\n\nHiding a thread does not block its author or change whether it is read. Each website keeps a pool of the 30 most recently hidden threads through refreshes and app restarts. Each hide expires after seven days. Hiding a 31st releases the oldest sooner so it can appear again; Undo restores a displaced hide with its original expiry time. Old hides without timestamps start their seven-day timer when this update first reads them. Other threads by the same author remain. Account → Privacy → Threads lists the pool newest first with a count out of 30 and Unhide for restoring them after Undo expires. Existing open tabs and direct links still work."),
            topic("Hide threads by an author","Hold an eligible thread on the board and choose Hide threads by this author. You can also tap an eligible author name inside a recent thread and choose Hide threads by this poster.\n\nAccount → Privacy → Authors lists the names you have hidden. Tap Unhide to show their threads again. This hides threads they started, not their replies inside other people's threads.\n\nAuthor-based hiding is unavailable in Search and By you, and for threads older than seven days, because older posting names can be randomized. Unknown authors may take a moment to be identified. Hidden-name settings are local to this app.")
        ),
        new Section("Reading threads","Reply structure, your posts, highlights and direct post links",
            topic("Optional inline reply previews","Open Account → Reading. Choose Jump links (Default), Nested cards or Stacked popovers, then Save reply preview mode. Jump links keeps the original behavior.\n\nNested cards opens a parent inside the current post. Tap the parent reference inside that preview to keep opening earlier replies. Tap an open reference again to collapse it and its deeper previews. Deep chains stop adding indentation so text stays readable.\n\nStacked popovers opens a parent above the thread. Tap its parent reference to continue. Back one or Android Back returns one preview. ×, tapping outside, or Android Back on the first preview closes it. Go to post closes the preview and jumps to that comment. Reading position in each stacked preview is retained when going back.\n\nPreviews use only posts already loaded and make no extra requests. Missing posts and circular references are handled without repeatedly opening them. Links, hold-link menus, text selection and holding the date to copy a post permalink remain available inside previews. The saved mode persists; open chains do not survive closing the app or leaving the thread. Same-thread refreshes and lazy post recycling retain valid open inline paths."),
            topic("Find text in a thread","Tap the three dots beside the thread title and choose Find in thread. Enter a word or phrase. Matching post-body text is highlighted without loading another page. Search ignores letter case and treats punctuation literally. Author names, dates and text inside external previews are not searched.\n\nThe search row stays below the top navigation. Use ‹ and › to jump between matches; 2/8 means the second of eight. Navigation wraps at either end. A 0/0 count means no matches. A + after the total means there are more than 10,000 matches; use a more specific phrase.\n\nTap × to close search and clear its highlights while keeping your current reading place. Android Back also closes search first; the header Back button still returns to the main page. Search stays through a refresh or rotation in the same thread, but clears when you leave the thread. It uses loaded post bodies only and makes no additional website requests."),
            topic("Follow replies and subthreads","Indented posts are replies within a conversation. The parent-author label above a reply identifies the post it answers. With the default Jump links mode, tap it to jump to that parent. Account → Reading offers optional Nested cards and Stacked popovers instead. Deeper chains show a depth label when indentation is capped.\n\nLandscape allows more indentation than portrait. Rotate the phone when following a deeply nested conversation.\n\nThe branch-rail and other proposed outline designs are not part of the current app."),
            topic("Find your posts and go to the top","Use ‹ and › beside Back to cycle through posts the website exposes as editable by you. The number between them shows the selected position, such as 1/4. The arrows wrap at either end.\n\nA 0/0 counter means the returned page contains no editable posts for your session. Detection uses the website's Edit controls, not matching a posting name.\n\nTap Top beside a post or at the thread footer to scroll to the start. Back returns to the main page, regardless of where you are in the thread."),
            topic("The subtle new-post tint","After a thread has been seen before, newly detected replies can receive a subtle tint. Your own editable posts are excluded. The first visit establishes a baseline rather than tinting every existing post.\n\nA tinted post waits until it is substantially on-screen for about one second, then fades back over about two seconds. Offscreen posts keep their indication until you view them.\n\nThis is separate from the red star on the main page: the star signals a higher reply count; the tint helps you spot individual new posts while reading."),
            topic("Copy a link to a specific post","Hold the date or an empty area of a post card to copy a direct link to that post. Link copied confirms it is in your clipboard. Paste it wherever you want.\n\nHold a link itself for link actions instead. Holding selectable message text uses Android's text selection, so use the post's date or blank card area when you want its permalink.")
        ),
        new Section("Posting & editing","New threads, replies, BB choices, edits and image uploads",
            topic("Input limits and validation","The inspected website forms allow titles up to 80 characters, new monikers up to 50, account names up to 100 and passwords up to 50. The app also reads length limits and required fields from returned forms before sending. The title and moniker fields show a counter. Pasted text and appended image links are never silently shortened; fix an over-limit value before submitting.\n\nLength uses browser UTF-16 counting, so an emoji can count as two characters. Messages preserve paragraph breaks and tabs. No message maximum is advertised by the inspected reply form; any maximum supplied by a future form is enforced. Blank bumps remain available where the website permits them.\n\nThese checks cover advertised form rules and malformed text, not unpublished server restrictions. The website can still reject a valid-looking submission for other reasons."),
            topic("Create a thread or reply","On the main page, tap New thread, enter a title and message, then tap Post. Creating a thread happens on one app page even if the website uses more than one form step.\n\nTo reply to a specific post, tap Reply on that post. To add a message directly to the thread, use the thread-level Reply control. Check the composer heading before sending.\n\nCancel returns without submitting. An unsent draft stays while you browse within the current app process, but closing the app discards it."),
            topic("BB and the quick-message choices","Tap BB to send a blank bump immediately. Hold BB, release, then tap a choice to send that short message. There is no second confirmation. Tap outside the choices or press Back to dismiss them without sending.\n\nThe choices are always alphabetized: 120, 180, cq, cr, mfcr, ntcr and tcr. Each sends that exact text.\n\nBB inside a post replies to that post. A thread-level BB adds a message to the thread. After submission, the app aims to keep your previous reading position rather than jump to the new message."),
            topic("Edit one of your posts","Tap Edit beside Reply when the website provides it. The editor loads the site's message text and subject. Make your changes and tap Save changes, or Cancel to leave without saving.\n\nThe app checks the current website form before saving. If the post changed since you opened it, it will refuse to overwrite the newer version.\n\nIf Edit is missing, check the website with the same account. The app cannot offer editing permission when the website does not expose it, even if you originally wrote the post."),
            topic("Upload images into a message","First set an ImgBB API key in Account → Uploads. Then open a reply or new-thread composer and tap the upload icon: an upward arrow above a tray.\n\nChoose one or several images. Up to 20 distinct JPEG, PNG, GIF or WebP images can be selected, with a 20 MB limit per image. Videos and documents are not supported by this uploader.\n\nCompleted URLs are appended to the end of your message and copied to the clipboard. The toast says image url in clipboard. You can move the URLs within your message before posting. Uploading an image does not submit the forum post."),
            topic("If an upload stops","Images upload one at a time. If you cancel or a file fails, completed image URLs remain in your message and clipboard; later files are not uploaded. Check those links before retrying to avoid unnecessary duplicates.\n\nIf access is refused, check the ImgBB key in Account → Uploads. Blank key fields do not reveal an existing key; saving a blank field retains it.\n\nUploaded images are sent to ImgBB and may be accessible to anyone with the returned link. Removing a URL from your draft does not delete the hosted image."),
            topic("If a post cannot be confirmed","The app does not automatically resend a post after an uncertain response. A request may have reached the website even if confirmation failed.\n\nFirst check By you or the destination thread to see whether the message appeared. If it did, do not send the same draft again.\n\nIf posting is locked after that check, use the recovery option shown in the warning or Account → Session → I've checked the previous post. Unlocking only permits a later manual submission; it does not resend anything.")
        ),
        new Section("Open threads","Open in the background, switch, close, restore and Undo",
            topic("Open another thread without leaving this one","Hold a board thread and choose Open in new tab. For a forum thread link inside a message, hold the link and choose Open in new tab.\n\nIt adds the thread to Open threads without switching to it or marking it read. Select that tab later to load it. Up to 12 threads can be kept open."),
            topic("Switch between open threads","Tap the open-threads button beside Account on the main page, or beside the own-post arrows inside a thread. Its count shows how many threads are open.\n\nThe bottom sheet lists your open threads. The current thread has a different background and a Current thread label. Tap another entry to open it and return to its saved reading position.\n\nTap Done or outside the sheet to dismiss it. Background tabs do not keep fetching replies; switching requests current content."),
            topic("Close a tab and undo a mistake","In Open threads, swipe an entry left or tap its × to close it. Closing the current thread returns to the main page.\n\nThe sheet offers Undo for about six seconds after a closure. Undo restores the most recently closed tab to its place in the list without switching to it.\n\nUndo applies only to the latest closure and does not survive restarting the app."),
            topic("Restore open threads after restarting","The app saves the list of open threads and their reading positions locally. After restarting, it starts on the main page with that list available in Open threads.\n\nTap a restored entry to fetch its current content and resume reading. The saved tab list is not an offline copy of the posts. Clearing app data or uninstalling removes it.")
        ),
        new Section("Links & media","Previews, albums, media sweep, zoom and browser fallback",
            topic("Tap or hold a link","Tap an external link in a post to open the full-screen preview. Tap × to close it and return to the thread.\n\nHold an external link for these choices, in order: Open in browser, Open preview, Copy link. Open in browser launches your ordinary browser. Open preview stays in the app.\n\nHolding a forum thread link also offers Open in new tab and Open thread. Links inside a full website/browser view may use that website's own long-press behavior."),
            topic("Images, albums, videos and PDFs","A single image opens in the image viewer. Recognized albums have previous/next arrows and an image counter. Use those to move through the album.\n\nVideos use a player when supported; tap Play to begin. Audio links can show an audio player. PDFs can have page arrows and a page counter. Provider support depends on what the remote site returns.\n\nSome links load a hosted preview or website instead. Deleted content, sign-in requirements and provider restrictions can prevent a native preview."),
            topic("Fit, Width, zoom and articles","For visual previews, use − and + to zoom and Fit to return to a contained view. Supported image viewers also allow pinch and dragging when enlarged. Width on hosted previews fills the available width and can require vertical scrolling.\n\nArticles use a reading layout with text and images in order. Their image-size controls resize article images; they do not zoom the entire article.\n\nAudio-only previews do not need visual zoom controls. The available controls depend on the preview type."),
            topic("Browse all media in a thread","Open the three-dot menu beside the thread title and choose Thread media. The number in that menu counts the collected media links, not the total number of images inside every album. A zero means no supported media links were collected.\n\nIt opens the normal preview with controls for moving between the thread's media links. Album navigation moves within an album; the thread-media navigation moves to another link.\n\nUse the post-jump action in that viewer to return to the post containing the link."),
            topic("Browser, Reader, Retry and Open original","When native extraction fails, the app can fall back to a website view in the preview. Browser also lets you open that view manually. Reader tries to turn the currently loaded page into the article reading layout.\n\nRetry tries the preview again. Open original sends the link to your external browser. If a video refuses to play or a site rejects an embedded browser, try Open original.\n\nWebsite mode can support ordinary sign-in and JavaScript, but does not guarantee access to subscriptions, verification-protected pages or removed content. External-site sessions are separate from your forum login.")
        ),
        new Section("Accounts & privacy","Saved logins, switching accounts, posting names and settings",
            topic("Lock the whole app","Open Account → Privacy → App lock and enable Require phone PIN to open AutoAdmit. This is off by default. Confirm your existing Android PIN, pattern or password to enable it. The app does not create or store a separate PIN. Set a phone screen lock in Android Settings first if you do not have one.\n\nWhen enabled, app content stays hidden until you unlock. Leaving AutoAdmit locks it again, including while opening an external browser or image picker. Canceling unlock leaves the app locked; tap Unlock to try again, or Exit to leave. Your reading position and in-memory draft remain. Returning from the image picker waits for unlock before starting its upload.\n\nScreenshots and recent-app previews are blocked while app lock is enabled. Turning it off in Account → Privacy → App lock also requires phone confirmation. Saved Accounts has its own separate PIN setting. Turn app lock off before removing your Android screen lock; the app cannot unlock without a device credential."),
            topic("Use the Account tabs","Login is for entering a website account name and password. Accounts manages stored login profiles. Moniker changes your public posting name. Session checks sign-in status and offers login/posting recovery.\n\nReading controls parent-reply previews. Theme groups presets, colors and scheduling. Uploads stores your ImgBB key. Privacy groups App lock, hidden Threads and hidden Authors. Updates checks a public GitHub repository for newer stable APK releases. Help is this offline guide. Swipe the category row sideways to reach more tabs.\n\nThe Website selector changes which site's account you are managing. It does not transfer a login from one site to the other."),
            topic("Unlock and switch saved accounts","Open Account → Accounts. If Require phone PIN is on, tap Unlock saved accounts. Confirm your phone PIN, pattern or password using Android's prompt. You need a secure phone screen lock. This is your phone's lock, not the website password or a separate app PIN.\n\nChoose a saved account, then tap Switch account. Selecting a name alone does not sign in. The current saved profile is marked Current.\n\nWhen Require phone PIN is on, leaving the Accounts tab or putting the app in the background locks it again. Accounts blocks screenshots whether the toggle is on or off. This protects the saved-account list; it does not lock the whole app or hide public posting names in threads."),
            topic("Give an account a private nickname","Open Account → Accounts and unlock if required. Choose a saved account, tap Nickname, enter a label such as Main or Alt and tap Save. The selector will show that nickname instead of the login name.\n\nNicknames are private labels stored encrypted on this phone. They never change your website login, password or public moniker, and are never sent to the website. Signing in again keeps the nickname.\n\nTap Nickname again to change it. Clear the field and Save to use the login name in the selector again. Nicknames are separate for each website; choose distinct nicknames within one website. Your actual login fields stay masked."),
            topic("Turn the Accounts PIN on or off","Open Account → Accounts and use Require phone PIN at the top. It starts on and applies to saved accounts for both websites.\n\nTurning it off asks Android to confirm your phone screen lock, if one is set. Canceling keeps PIN protection on. If the phone has no secure screen lock, you can turn the requirement off without a phone-unlock prompt.\n\nWith PIN off, anyone using the app can view, switch or remove saved profiles without another unlock. Credentials stay encrypted and Accounts still blocks screenshots. Turning the requirement back on locks Accounts immediately. Your choice stays through app restarts and ordinary updates."),
            topic("Add or remove a saved login","In Login, enter both fields, leave Save login securely on this phone checked and sign in. A successful saved login adds or updates that profile for the selected website. In unlocked Accounts, Add account also lets you enter another login.\n\nTo remove one, choose it in Accounts and tap Remove, then confirm. Removing an inactive profile keeps your current session. Removing the current saved profile clears its local session too.\n\nSession → Forget current login removes only the current saved profile and local session. Other profiles remain. None of these actions deletes a website account."),
            topic("Change your posting name","Open Account → Moniker. Your current moniker is selected automatically when it can be identified. To reuse a name, select it under Current / previous monikers and tap Use selected name. To create one, enter New posting name and tap Create and use name.\n\nThis changes your public posting name on the website, not the account name used to sign in. The site sets the allowed length and available previous names.\n\nIf the change cannot be confirmed, check the website before trying again. A name change does not submit a forum post."),
            topic("Saved fields, automatic sign-in and local data","Stars in saved login fields are placeholders; your actual credentials are not prefilled. Enter both fields to use another manual login, or unlock Accounts to use a stored profile.\n\nCredentials and cookies are encrypted in private app storage. The active saved profile's automatic-sign-in option lets the app try to restore an expired session; other saved profiles are not tried in a loop. Failed automatic sign-in needs attention in Account.\n\nLocal history, hidden names, tabs and saved logins are specific to this app installation. They do not automatically sync with the Firefox extension or another phone. Help contains no account-specific information.")
        ),
        new Section("Fixing problems","Missing stars, sign-in trouble, slow previews and lost permissions",
            topic("I have not seen a red star","Stars need a read baseline in this app and a later detected increase in the reply count. Simply opening a new thread, looking up its author, or reading it only in a browser does not create that comparison.\n\nOpen a thread here, then return to the board. Later replies can produce a star after the visible list refreshes. Opening it or swiping it away in New replies marks that displayed count read.\n\nThe app checks while in the foreground; it is not a background push-notification service."),
            topic("Sign-in or a posting name is wrong","Check the Website selector and Account → Session → Check session. If signed out, enter your login again or unlock Accounts and switch to the intended profile. A website can revoke or expire an existing session.\n\nIf a browser is signed in but the app is not, sign in separately in the app. Browser cookies are not imported.\n\nFor a public posting name, use Account → Moniker. Changing a saved login username is not how you change the name shown on posts."),
            topic("A preview is blank, slow or will not play","Give it time to finish loading; a timeout may be retried once. If the native preview fails, try Browser, or Open original to use your normal browser.\n\nA site may require sign-in, JavaScript, verification or an active subscription. A link can also be deleted or broken. A preview cannot guarantee every provider will work.\n\nIf the preview stays stuck, close it with × and reopen it. Your reading position stays in the thread. For an upload problem, use Posting & editing → If an upload stops."),
            topic("Edit is missing or my posts show 0/0","The app shows Edit and counts your posts only when the website's returned page exposes the corresponding Edit links. Randomized posting names do not decide ownership.\n\nCheck you are signed in to the correct site and account. Compare the same post on the website. If the website does not show Edit either, the app cannot restore that permission.\n\nPull to refresh after signing in again. Account changes can change which posts are editable."),
            topic("Check for app updates","Open Account → Updates. The official public repository is selected by default. Use official repository restores it after a custom or blank setting. You can enter another public owner/repository or its HTTPS URL and tap Save update repository; clear and save it to disable the source. Tap Check for updates to look for the latest stable release, or Choose version to browse stable releases with APKs. More releases loads the next page. Installed and older versions are labelled for reference; only newer builds can update without removing app data. No checks run automatically. Review the release notes, then tap Download. The app checks the APK package, newer Android version code, signing identity and any supplied SHA-256 checksum before handing it to Android. Android asks you to approve installation. If asked to allow updates from AutoAdmit, enable it, return and tap Install downloaded update. Do not uninstall; updates preserve app data. No GitHub password or token is needed. The repository must publish a stable numeric release tag and attach a signed AutoAdmit.apk. Private repositories, drafts and prereleases are not supported."),
            topic("I cannot unlock Accounts","Use the phone screen-lock PIN, pattern or password, not your forum password. If the phone has no secure screen lock, set one in Android Settings first, or turn Require phone PIN off in Accounts.\n\nCanceling Android's prompt leaves the list locked. Reopen Accounts and tap Unlock saved accounts to try again.\n\nManual login remains available in Login. The Accounts lock does not stop the already signed-in session from browsing or automatically maintaining its login.")
        )
    };
}
